.TH ADBDECK 1 "" "adbdeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adbdeck \- desktop companion for Android Debug Bridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adbdeck
[\fB\-d\fR | \fB\-\-daemon\fR] [\fIAPK\fR...]
.br
.B adbdeck
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-V\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adbdeck
is a graphical application for working with Android devices through
.BR adb (1):
device overview, file browser, app manager, process and performance monitors,
shell, logcat, screenshots, screen mirroring, wireless pairing and more.
The adb program must be installed.
.PP
APK files given on the command line are queued for installation on the selected device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run without a window and keep remembered devices connected: phones that were connected
before are reconnected on Wi-Fi (including phones advertising Wireless debugging), at their
saved addresses, and on the gateways of the local networks (USB tethering, hotspot).
Only one such service runs per user. It stops when automatic reconnection or the background
service is switched off in Settings. The window starts this service at login through an
autostart entry while the setting is on.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/adbdeck/settings.toml
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/adbdeck/data.json
Remembered devices and window state.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/adbdeck-daemon.desktop
Starts the background service at login. Written and removed by Settings.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/adbdeck-daemon.service
The same service as a systemd user unit. Enable it with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now adbdeck-daemon" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log level, for example
.BR adbdeck=debug .
The default is
.BR adbdeck=info .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR adb (1)
